# Karpathy Guidelines

Apply these guidelines with project-specific instructions. Prefer the more specific rule when they conflict and state the choice.

## Think Before Coding

- State assumptions and material ambiguity before implementation.
- Present alternatives instead of choosing silently.
- Name a simpler approach when one exists.
- Stop and ask when missing information changes the work.

## Simplicity First

- Build the smallest solution that meets the request.
- Avoid speculative features, abstractions, configuration, and impossible-case handling.

## Surgical Changes

- Change only lines that trace to the request.
- Preserve unrelated code, comments, formatting, and conventions.
- Remove only unused code made obsolete by the current change.

## Goal-Driven Execution

- Define observable success criteria before implementation.
- Reproduce bugs before fixing them when practical.
- Verify relevant tests and report skipped checks.
